.TH OMORFOS\-SESSION 1 "" omorfos "omorfos manual"
.nh
.ad l
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
omorfos\-session \- What an omorfos session does besides draw: locking before sleep, starting programs at login, the volume, the brightness and what is playing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBomorfos\-session [COMMAND]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Without a command it watches over the session for as long as it lasts, locking the screen before the machine sleeps; the compositor starts it so at login. With one, it does what a key or the menu asks, and can be bound to keys in keys.yaml as \fBspawn: [omorfos\-session, volume, up]\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBvolume up|down|mute\fR
Turn the sound that plays up or down by five hundredths, or mute it and back
.TP
\fBmicrophone mute\fR
Mute the microphone, or hear it again
.TP
\fBbrightness up|down\fR
Make the screen a twentieth brighter or darker, never quite dark
.TP
\fBmedia play\-pause\fR
Tell the player that is playing, or else one that is paused, to play or to pause
.TP
\fBmedia next|previous|stop\fR
Tell it to go on to the next, back to the one before, or stop
.TP
\fBsleep|restart|shut\-down\fR
Ask logind for the machine to sleep, start again or turn off
.TP
\fBlog\-out\fR
End the session, as the compositor ends it
.TP
\fBoffered\fR
Print which of sleep, restart, shut\-down and log\-out a locked screen may offer, and what holds the machine
.TP
\fBautostart\fR
Start what is to start with the session, as at login
.TP
\fBforget ssh|gpg...\fR
Have ssh\-agent forget its keys, or gpg\-agent its passphrases
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-locked\fR
With sleep, restart or shut\-down: asked from a locked screen, so done only where no password is asked for
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print this help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print the version
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
omorfos\-session volume up
omorfos\-session media next
omorfos\-session forget ssh gpg
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBomorfos\fR(1), \fBomorfosctl\fR(1), \fBomorfos\-config\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-keys\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-rules\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-menu\fR(5), \fBomorfos\-theme\fR(5)
